description: Canonical data ownership, relations, timezone, and write paths
alwaysApply: true
---

# Data invariants

- Path: Company → Project → WorkItem → TimeEntry. Project/Company labels come from relations, not copied text on child rows.
- Multiple Company profiles may exist; every Project belongs to exactly one Company. `Project.companyId` may be nullable only during the Dhas backfill; no orphans before NOT NULL.
- TimeEntry must reference an existing WorkItem. `projectId` must equal that WorkItem's project (or be derived). Reject mismatch with 400/409; do not write the row.
- Owner identity is resolved server-side. Never trust browser `userId` or `assigneeId` to switch users. Assignee and Daily Work logger are the same owner.
- Identity standard is `05-record-identifiers.mdc`: internal numeric PK/FK, immutable random UUID public_id for client references. API relations resolve public UUIDs to authorized numeric keys; imported IDs and provider IDs stay separate namespaces.
- Board columns are `WorkItem.status`. No private board records. Status writes go through the WorkItem service used by `/work-items`.
- Dashboard, Analysis, and Project summaries use the shared metric formulas. Never hard-code sample arrays or treat API errors as zero.
- System default time zone is `Asia/Bangkok` in every environment, including application and database sessions. Use it for date-only values, calendar/year boundaries, business dates, filters, date groups, and every timestamp written to the database. Do not convert stored values to UTC or infer dates from the browser/device timezone.
- Database date-only values represent Bangkok calendar dates. Database timestamps represent Bangkok local wall-clock date/time; use explicit Bangkok conversions at API/UI boundaries and configure database sessions to `Asia/Bangkok` so database defaults such as `now()` follow the same rule.
- Settings may display the fixed system timezone `Asia/Bangkok`; do not expose a timezone override preference.
- Do not rely on implicit cascade for business history. Project deletion must be blocked while WorkItems, TimeEntries, or dependent history exists.
- GitLab import upserts the same `WorkItem`. Company comes from the mapped PMS Project. Removing a mapping keeps imported WorkItems and TimeEntries.
- Related-row mutations commit in one transaction. After success, refresh or invalidate every surface that reads those rows.
